From: Noswad <64293615+TheNoswad@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:15:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: max17042: measure temperature when TEx is left
 set

The max77759 fuel gauge on Pixel 6 comes up with Config.TEx set, so
Temp holds whatever the host last wrote (22.0 C) and never changes.
Nothing in Linux writes it. Clear TEx so the gauge converts the battery
thermistor itself; verified on oriole: idle ~44 C, falls 4.4 C in 3 min
in a fridge while the SoC TMU moves 1 C.
---
 drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c b/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c
index d409d2f0d..61d447fe9 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c
@@ -38,6 +38,7 @@
 
 /* Interrupt mask bits */
 #define CFG_ALRT_BIT_ENBL	(1 << 2)
+#define CFG_TEX_BIT		(1 << 8)
 #define CFG2_DSOCI_BIT_ENBL	(1 << 7)
 
 #define VFSOC0_LOCK		0x0000
@@ -1201,6 +1202,18 @@ static int max17042_probe(struct i2c_client *client, struct device *dev, int irq
 	dev_dbg(dev, "task period: %#.4x (%d)\n", chip->task_period,
 		chip->task_period);
 
+	/*
+	 * Config.TEx makes the gauge wait for the host to write Temp. This
+	 * driver never does, so the reported temperature would stay frozen at
+	 * whatever was last written (22.0 C on Pixel 6, where firmware leaves
+	 * TEx set). Let the gauge convert its thermistor input instead.
+	 */
+	regmap_read(chip->regmap, MAX17042_CONFIG, &val);
+	if (val & CFG_TEX_BIT) {
+		dev_info(dev, "clearing Config.TEx, measuring temperature\n");
+		regmap_update_bits(chip->regmap, MAX17042_CONFIG, CFG_TEX_BIT, 0);
+	}
+
 	chip->battery = devm_power_supply_register(dev, max17042_desc,
 						   &psy_cfg);
 	if (IS_ERR(chip->battery))
